1
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,160
Get up, get up.

2
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:16,840
Sis, this one tastes good.

3
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,000
I don’t want it.

4
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:18,720
Just give it a try.

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:19,600
I don’t want it, you try it.

6
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:20,240
I said I don’t want it.

7
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:20,800
No way.

8
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,120
We can’t let Qi Dongdong interrupt our date.

9
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:24,120
I’m going to pack up the tent.

10
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:25,400
Alright then.

11
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:29,960
Dongdong.

12
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,040
Don’t you have class today?

13
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:32,720
Nope.

14
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,800
I’ve already started my internship.

15
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:34,720
Then,

16
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,960
didn’t you say you were going to start a business?

17
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,760
Shouldn’t you be preparing or doing some research?

18
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:39,680
No need.

19
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:40,800
Dongdong.

20
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,560
How can you be so unserious?

21
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:47,000
With this kind of half-hearted attitude,

22
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,200
how can you possibly succeed?

23
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:50,920
Wow, bro, you’ve gotten good at sayings.

24
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,240
I’m just taking one day off.

25
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,080
It really doesn’t matter.

26
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,000
How can it not matter?

27
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,120
Every minute you slack off,

28
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,520
others are making leaps ahead.

29
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,400
But I want to be with my sister—

30
00:00:59,480 --> 00:00:59,920
No.

31
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:00,760
You don’t want to.

32
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:05,640
Brother-in-law, I get it now.

33
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:06,480
Don’t worry.

34
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:07,400
I will definitely work hard.

35
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:10,279
Have fun with my sister.

36
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,880
Finally, no one’s interrupting us.

37
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:18,520
Why did he leave?

38
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:19,760
Well,

39
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,040
he had something to do and left earlier.

40
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:24,400
Qi Miao,

41
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:25,160
let me tell you—

42
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:26,040
Qi Miao.

43
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:31,320
Why are they here?

44
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:33,720
I arranged to meet Jian Dan.

45
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:34,160
And besides,

46
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:35,800
how can you go out and have fun without Jian Dan?

47
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:38,880
Qi Xiaomiao.

48
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,480
Jian Dan, you're here.

49
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:41,960
Your dress looks really nice.

50
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,160
Let's take a picture together later.

51
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,440
Sure, sure!

52
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:53,600
Why do you look upset?

53
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:54,960
I'm not.

54
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:59,320
It's written all over your face.

55
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:02,560
I said I'm not.

56
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:05,320
Alright.

57
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,080
I was just thinking about yesterday, Ai Yite...

58
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,160
You know, after his confession failed.

59
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,760
I figured I'd bring them out to lift their spirits.

60
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:12,120
Besides, we have plenty of days to spend together.

61
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:13,120
And...

62
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,239
It's more fun with more people.

63
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,200
Alright then.

64
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:18,360
My girlfriend,

65
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,560
As long as you're happy,

66
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:20,560
I’ll do anything.

67
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:24,240
Where did you learn to talk like a domineering CEO?

68
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,720
I didn’t learn this from anywhere.

69
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,040
This is just how I talk.

70
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:29,200
Isn't that how they portray it in TV dramas?

71
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,280
Watch fewer cheesy dramas from now on.

72
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:32,120
Lines like these...

73
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:32,960
I don't even write them anymore.

74
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:36,640
Remember.

75
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:38,680
I won't let you escape.

76
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:40,720
If you must run,

77
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:42,920
you can only run into my arms.

78
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:44,880
Yes, yes.

79
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:46,200
My dearest Star Envoy,

80
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,480
Please spare me!

81
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,840
If you’re wrong, just take your punishment obediently.

82
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:55,840
Is it tasty?

83
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:56,840
Is it good?

84
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:59,320
I grilled this using my secret recipe.

85
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,480
Give it a try.

86
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:03,640
Uh...

87
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,800
I’m gonna go chat with Jian Dan for a bit.

88
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:06,720
You guys carry on.

89
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,280
I shouldn’t have meddled in your affairs yesterday.

90
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:17,480
I've made up my mind.

91
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,280
Since we’re both staying on Earth,

92
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:21,720
I'm determined to win Jian Dan over.

93
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:25,840
There's a saying on Earth, isn't there?

94
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:29,160
If love can last forever,

95
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:31,400
does it matter if we're together every single day?

96
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,040
Every single day and night.

97
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,360
That's quite a good phrase,

98
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:40,160
I should jot it down.

99
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,000
But Haoruichi,

100
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,760
if you decide to stay on Earth,

101
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,760
there's something you must know.

102
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,040
Cheers!

103
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:05,600
Just drinking like this is way too boring.

104
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:06,520
Why don't we play a game?

105
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:07,440
Sure! Sounds good!

106
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,320
What should we play?

107
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:09,920
How about rock-paper-scissors?

108
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:12,080
The winner gets to ask any question,

109
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,560
and the loser...

110
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,080
the loser drinks.

111
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,720
Any question is allowed?

112
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:18,480
Of course!

113
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:21,240
And they must answer truthfully.

114
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:22,480
Wait a second.

115
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:24,080
What are you planning?

116
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:24,720
Don't worry about it.

117
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:25,360
Come on, come on.

118
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,119
With my lucky attribute as Blue Kexingshi,

119
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:29,720
this little game is a piece of cake.

120
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,640
Rock, paper, scissors!

121
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,160
You lost! Drink up! Drink, drink!

122
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:38,600
No way!

123
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,240
He... he can't drink.

124
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,680
How about I drink for him?

125
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,000
Qi Xiaomiao,

126
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:46,840
every time I tell you to drink, you avoid it.

127
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:49,040
But now, for this man...

128
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,280
Sigh, beauty really is a trap.

129
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,640
If you can't drink,

130
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,840
I can drink on your behalf.

131
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:55,960
Get lost!

132
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:56,720
Alright.

133
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,000
It's fine.

134
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,200
I can drink.

135
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:03,360
I'll win next round for sure.

136
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:10,160
Here we go again! Rock, paper, scissors!

137
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,280
Rock, paper, scissors!

138
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,560
Rock, paper, scissors!

139
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:17,080
I won!

140
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,800
Can I ask a question now?

141
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:20,960
Aiyet, I'm warning you.

142
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:21,800
What's going on?

143
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,800
If you dare to ask something weird...

144
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,640
Why am I losing again?

145
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:24,560
You know what will happen to you.

146
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,040
Actually...

147
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,800
I just wanted to ask you...

148
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:31,720
What is your ideal kind of love?

149
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,280
Don’t be fooled by how loud and carefree she usually seems.

150
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,200
Actually...

151
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:37,240
She has never been in a relationship since she was a kid.

152
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,280
You've never been in a relationship?

153
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,280
So what?

154
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,000
Is it a problem?

155
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:45,000
No wonder when I confessed to you last time...

156
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,080
You were so shy.

157
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:46,880
So...

158
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:49,280
What do you think of me?

159
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,120
That’s your second question.

160
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,280
I have the right not to answer.

161
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:54,360
Come on, come on.

162
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,360
Let's do it again.

163
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:57,360
One more time.

164
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:01,800
There's no more wine.

165
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,800
I'll go get some more.

166
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,560
How did the two of them end up kissing?

167
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:22,840
I...

168
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:23,800
I didn’t mean to.

169
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:24,440
I slipped.

170
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,200
Aiyet!

171
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,240
You’re done for!

172
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,200
I... I really...

173
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,520
I didn’t mean to!

174
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,440
Stand right there!

175
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,280
I’ll beat you! I really didn’t mean to!

176
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:37,440
Finally, no one’s disturbing us.

177
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,600
Qi Miao...

178
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:42,720
I haven’t finished...

179
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,160
My wish yet.

180
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:34,520
One, two, three...

181
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:43,400
Morning!

182
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:46,960
Morning!

183
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,640
Why are you in my tent?

184
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,320
You asked me to stay last night.

185
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:05,280
When did I say that?

186
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:05,960
You did say it.

187
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,480
You literally said it yourself last night.

188
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,560
Eit!

189
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,000
You’re so dead today.

190
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:12,720
Howie!

191
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,680
Stop right there!

192
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,600
Are you okay?

193
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,160
Sorry about that!

194
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:22,840
It’s fine.

195
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:24,880
Miaomiao.

196
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:27,480
Why is Howie bleeding blue from his nose?

197
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,480
Oh, that’s simple.

198
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:31,000
I’ll explain it to you later.

199
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,000
What’s wrong?

200
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:37,440
Howie!

201
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:38,320
What’s wrong with you, Howie?

202
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,400
Howie! Howie!

203
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,120
Howie!

204
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:40,959
Howie!

205
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:58,960
Qi Miao!

206
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:02,160
Now, are you finally going to behave?
